    "prompt": "An international team used viral vectors to boost production of the secreted form of the Klotho protein in middle-aged mice. The treated mice lived 15 to 20 percent longer and showed improvements in muscle strength, bone density and cognitive performance. Researchers observed increased formation of neurons and enhanced immune activity in the hippocampus. They filed patents for using Klotho to treat bone, muscle and aging-related deficits and suggested that with a suitable delivery method, this gene therapy could help build a healthier society by combating age-related decline.\n",
    "context": "Strong animal evidence for a specific biological mechanism, but the leap to human\ntherapeutic claims and societal benefits is speculative. Classic mechanism vs evidence gap.\n",
